# Knowledge-Learning Cursor Rules

## Source-Grounding
- STRICT_SOURCE_MODE is enabled by default
- Material facts and verified locations include [Source: ...] citations
- Mark user goals/background as user-provided and route design as planning advice
- Mark unverified claims with [unverified]

## Learning Workflow
- Uploads and /import first build a lightweight material map, not whole-book notes
- Show the chapter map, then ask only for missing goals, background and studied chapters
- Use /learn [topic] --plan [--material <path>] for a source-grounded chapter route
- Save MATERIAL_INDEX.md and LEARNING_PATH.md in projects/<教材或主题>/
- No default daily calendar; distinguish verified prerequisites from suggested order
- Learn with /learn or /study
- Review with /review and /flashcard
- Track progress with /track

## Note Format
- Atomic notes with YAML frontmatter
- Include source, tags, domain, and confidence fields
- Use [[wiki-link]] for connections
